322:<h3>The team left three sources that disagree</h3>
329:<p>These disagree in places. The revival changes the team's Fortress for one of two reasons only: two of these sources contradict each other, or a program fails. It reconciles them. Where the team's later work, in the compiler's library or the type papers, departs from the original specification, the revival follows the later work. It then updates the specification to match what it implements. A callout marks the passage, and Appendix I keeps the original text with the reason.</p>
353:<li>Original: one sentence of the Working Draft forbids this. The 1.0 release of March 2008 doesn't have it. In git, the sentence first appears in the specification's sources as Sukyoung Ryu re-imported them in November 2009. Neither implementation enforced it. The checker implements the type group's model of 2011, from their OOPSLA paper, which allows such overloads.</li>
